# =====================================================================
# Project 23 — Agentic Analyst
#
# NOTE ON CASE: the data folder is lowercase `data/`, matching the paths
# hardcoded throughout the code. It was `Data/` once; Windows didn't care
# but the Linux CI runner did, and every database test failed with
# "unable to open database file". Both spellings are listed below as
# insurance — don't remove the capitalised copies.
#
# What we DO commit, deliberately, is listed at the bottom. Read that
# before adding anything here.
# =====================================================================

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json

# --- python ----------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- raw Spider download (1.8 GB) ------------------------------------
# The only genuinely large thing here. Rebuild with:
#     python data_prep/prepare_spider.py
data/spider_data/
Data/spider_data/

# --- generated databases & charts ------------------------------------
# The three Spider databases ARE committed (see the bottom of this file).
# These two are not: create_db.py builds them, and tools/sql_tools.py calls
# it automatically through _ensure_db_exists() when they are missing.
# Verified — delete both, make one run_sql() call, and they come back.
data/db/analytics.db
data.db
*.sqlite
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
data/charts/*.png

# --- demo trajectories -------------------------------------------------
# demo_workflow.py and the UI write synthetic runs against analytics.db
# into data/trajectories/, named plain YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl. They are
# regenerable, and they must never be confused with the real Spider runs.
#
# This bit matters: label_dataset.py reads *-train.jsonl only, so demo
# output cannot reach the critic's training set even if someone commits it
# anyway. The rule below is the second line of defence, not the first.
data/trajectories/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9].jsonl

# --- large model weights ---------------------------------------------
# The LightGBM critic is 2.6 MB and IS committed. These are not.
checkpoints/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.onnx

# Fine-tuned text critics: ~270 MB for distilbert, ~600 MB for ModernBERT.
# The weights stay out — `python scripts/train_bert.py` rebuilds them in a
# few minutes.
models/critic_bert_*/*

# ...but meta.json IS committed. 2 KB recording the model id, input format,
# max_len, learning rate, epochs, seed and validation score behind each
# result. The weights are reproducible; the record of what was actually run
# is not, and it is the thing that makes a reported number checkable.
!models/critic_bert_*/meta.json

# --- runtime output --------------------------------------------------
server.log
*.log
data/uploads/

# The complexity router retrains itself at server startup, so this is
# regenerated output rather than a deliverable. The critic models are
# committed because they take minutes to train and are pinned to reported
# numbers; this one takes seconds and isn't.
models/router_model.joblib

# --- os / editor -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
__MACOSX/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp


# =====================================================================
# DELIBERATELY COMMITTED — do not add these to the rules above
# =====================================================================
#
# data/db/*.db                 11 MB, all three Spider databases.
#                              chinook_1 is required by the test suite,
#                              so CI fails without it. college_2 and
#                              formula_1 hold 120 of the 150 questions.
#                              Committing them means no teammate ever
#                              needs the 1.8 GB Spider download.
#
# data/tasks/*.json            216 KB. Everyone must run the identical
#                              150 questions or our numbers are not
#                              comparable across layers.
#
# data/trajectories/*.jsonl    10.2 MB, two files, NOT reproducible —
#                              sampled at temperature 0.7, so those exact
#                              runs are gone forever if lost.
#                                -train.jsonl        1,620 runs, the
#                                                    critic's training set
#                                -superseded.jsonl      80 runs, pre-fix
#                                                    baseline (9.2% solve
#                                                    rate vs 30.9%), kept
#                                                    as evidence
#                              DO NOT MERGE OR RENAME THESE — the
#                              exclusion is by filename. See README.
#
# data/critic/*.parquet        889 KB. Derived, but it pins the exact
#                              table behind the reported numbers.
#
# data/critic/split.json       The frozen train/test split. Must be
#                              identical for everyone or results drift.
#
# models/critic_*.joblib       2.6 MB, so A, C and D can load the critic
#                              without retraining it.
#
# notebooks/*.ipynb            Committed WITH their outputs. The charts
#                              are the results record — a reviewer
#                              cloning this repo should see them without
#                              a GPU. Normally you would strip outputs;
#                              this is a deliberate exception.
#
# If any of these grows past ~50 MB, reconsider — but move it to Git LFS
# rather than silently dropping it.
